sitive and negative grades. Using a real-basis multiplication map on the positive space yields the usual complex tensor product; the negative branch followed by the B-plane reflection encodes v_A tensor conjugate(v_B). An ordinary Z on the real/imaginary coordinate is a physical orthogonal operation on that local real representation. Undoing arbitrary conjugation as a complex channel relative to an already fixed external complex spectator would act as a transpose on the system density and fail complete positivity. These statements concern different interfaces. Known real data, known state-specific corrections, or encoding logical data after aligning blank resource registers evade that data obstruction. Operations commuting with common J preserve the chosen space; generic physically real local operations need not preserve the code.","locality":"Contact Q acts on the two transported plane coordinates. Local controlled correction on B in this implementation includes its sheet, which must travel with it or receive the classical grade at B; if reflection uses only nearest sheet hops, reflecting every coordinate around 0 can cost order q in sheet diameter. Causal rows suppose unit-speed base transport, permitted local storage, and instantaneous on-site comparison/gates. At separation D first joint light cones overlap at ceil(D/2) ticks, or D if B stays at home. Returned outputs and flags are available at both homes by 2 ceil(D/2) ticks for the midpoint schedule. Exact mandatory one-step walkers starting at odd separation have opposite parity forever at equal times unless a hold, offset launch time or adjacent-edge contact is supplied. Shared preexisting correlations can align selected records but furnish neither an instantaneous signaling operation nor a transport-free remote Q.","prior_work":["A_rational_plane_for_cyclic_phase.md","Records_and_complex_structure.md"]}
